  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "Bun.serve's routes table is an object literal whose keys are quoted route strings. Measured with dump_call_emissions: omega-javascript and omega-typescript emit no fact at all for a string-keyed property, whether its value is an identifier, an arrow function or a method body, so neither the route URL nor the handler it names is stated. Bun therefore has no http:{method}:{route} key space -- the server is addressed by its declaration site and nothing below it is in the graph.",
      "Bun.serve's fetch/websocket/error handlers are object-literal properties. omega-javascript emits definition.method for an identifier-keyed property, omega-typescript only for the shorthand method form, and in neither case does any span or field relate that property to the serve call, whose span is the six bytes of the member name. Which function answers a request is not stated.",
      "call.constructor carries no fields in any JS/TS Pack -- the canonical call view is published on call.function and call.method only -- so new Database(\"app.sqlite\") names no database file and a SQLite database is addressed by the position of its constructor.",
      "Bun.env and process.env are member references, not calls, and no JS/TS Pack emits a fact for a bare member reference, so which environment variables a Bun project reads cannot be answered.",
      "bunfig.toml setting values are published by omega-toml as attributes, which the overlay cannot read, so a BunConfigSetting names install.registry but cannot say what registry."
    ]
  },
